As an example, suppose that we need to compute n values and add them together. We know that this can be done with the following serial code:
sum = 0;
for ( i = 0; i < n ; i++) {
x = Compute_next_value ( . . . ) ; sum += x ; }
Now suppose we also have p cores and p ≤ n. Then each core can form a partial sum of approximately n/p values:
